## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the circuit breaker in staging with load ramps?
- How to adjust SLO targets when external dependency quality changes?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes a beginner-friendly angle on data integrity under deploy pressure, focusing on per-tenant observability, controlled backpressure, and data replay safety.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant observability: lag, offsets, retry counts
- Ingress throttling and traffic-splitting
- Idempotent processing and dedup keys
- Rollback and data validation windows

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple deduplicated idempotent processor
const seen = new Set();
function handle(event){
  const id = event.tenant + ":" + event.id;
  if (seen.has(id)) return;
  seen.add(id);
  // process event
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the rollback plan in a staging env?
- What telemetry would you add to verify data integrity after rollback?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical incident engineering: how to fuse disparate signals, assign accountability, and make safe change decisions under pressure.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-signal correlation across metrics/logs/traces
- SLO-aligned alert routing and ownership mapping
- Canary and synthetic testing for regression prevention
- RCA templating and rollback playbooks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple rule mapping alerts to on-call owners
const owners = {
  payments: "team-payments",
  auth: "team-auth",
  inventory: "team-inventory"
};
function route(alert) {
  const svc = alert.tags?.service || "general";
  return owners[svc] || "oncall";
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the end-to-end runbook in a staging environment?
- What metrics would you collect to validate the success of the rollback strategy?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to handle clock skew and scheduling drift in a regulated batch pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- Clock synchronization, idempotent batch processing, per-tenant isolation
- Safe backfill, read-after-write consistency, and rollback criteria
- Clear observability and thresholds for cross-region workloads

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo dedupe example
async function processBatch(batchId, tenantId, payload){
  const key = `${batchId}:${tenantId}`;
  const exists = await redis.setnx(`dedup:${key}`, '1');
  if(!exists) return; // already processed
  // process
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the backfill strategy without impacting live tenants?
- What if clock drift persists after NTP sync—what changes to the plan would you add?
